# What is NOT here matters as much as what is: `Cargo.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`,
# and `rust-toolchain.toml` are all committed on purpose. A benchmark claim is
# only reproducible if the dependency versions behind it are pinned.

# --- Rust -------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# cargo-fuzz (M1). The corpus IS committed — a fuzzing corpus that took CPU
# hours to grow is a build artefact worth keeping. Crashes and the build tree
# are not.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/coverage

# --- Node / extension -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
packages/extension/dist/

# Store upload bundles (M7)
*.zip

# Generated by `pnpm build:wasm` from crates/leviathan-wasm. Never committed:
# it is compiler output, and a stale copy in git is worse than no copy.
packages/extension/src/wasm/

# --- Test data --------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated fixtures, up to 500 MB each. Reproduced by `leviathan-cli fixtures`
# (M1) or the snippets in USER_MANUAL.md §3.4.
/fixtures/generated/

# --- Local environment ------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.log
!*/src/**/*.log

# Per-machine tool permissions. `.claude/settings.json` (shared project config)
# is committed; the `.local` override is not — it differs per contributor.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

